WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Press play. Subtitles appear.
200+ languages. One app:  tryray.app

2
00:00:30.239 --> 00:00:33.325
All men's souls are immortal.

3
00:00:34.117 --> 00:00:37.454
but the souls of the righteous
are immortal and divine.
-Socrates.

4
00:01:53.405 --> 00:01:55.365
Hyperion!

5
00:02:36.073 --> 00:02:39.660
My oracle ... what vision did you dream?

6
00:02:42.412 --> 00:02:45.749
Titans... unleashed.

7
00:02:46.875 --> 00:02:48.544
By whom?

8
00:02:50.087 --> 00:02:52.548
King Hyperion.

9
00:02:54.967 --> 00:03:00.264
He seeks the Bow of Epirus to rule over mankind.

10
00:03:03.225 --> 00:03:05.060
We must pray.

11
00:03:15.696 --> 00:03:19.491
When this world was still young

12
00:03:20.576 --> 00:03:26.164
long before man or beast roamed
these lands.

13
00:03:26.373 --> 00:03:28.625
Immortals: The War gods

14
00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:32.754
There was a war in the Heavens.

15
00:03:33.338 --> 00:03:38.468
Immortals. once thought
incapable of death.

16
00:03:38.468 --> 00:03:42.681
discovered they had the power
to kill one another.

17
00:03:42.931 --> 00:03:48.687
Lost in this war.
was a weapon of unimaginable power:

18
00:03:48.937 --> 00:03:50.939
The Epirus Bow.

19
00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:55.235
The victors declared themselves
Gods.

20
00:03:55.527 --> 00:03:59.489
While the vanquished were
renamed Titans

21
00:03:59.698 --> 00:04:04.286
and forever imprisoned within the
bowels of Mount Tartarus.

22
00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:09.875
Eons passed.
Mankind flourished...

23
00:04:10.167 --> 00:04:14.129
..And the great war receeded
from memory.

24
00:04:16.632 --> 00:04:21.470
But the evil that once was...

25
00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:26.767
...has reemerged.

26
00:04:35.442 --> 00:04:40.822
Hyperion is here. He comes for me.

27
00:04:42.574 --> 00:04:44.326
We must go now.

28
00:04:46.828 --> 00:04:51.792
SYBELLINE MONASTERY
GREECE. 1228 BC.

29
00:05:06.390 --> 00:05:09.726
Stop! You cannot enter here.
This is sacred ground!

30
00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:12.771
Sacred for whom?

31
00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:15.482
What do you want with us?

32
00:05:16.483 --> 00:05:19.111
Where is the virgin Oracle?

33
00:05:22.447 --> 00:05:27.703
Defile this house further and
you will risk the wrath of the gods.

34
00:05:29.955 --> 00:05:32.583
The Gods...

35
00:05:35.919 --> 00:05:38.547
Gods...

36
00:05:39.214 --> 00:05:44.469
The Gods? Go ahead. call upon them.

37
00:05:44.761 --> 00:05:48.807
Pray... Ask for their help...

38
00:05:49.683 --> 00:05:54.104
Pray to the same Gods
who idly stood by

39
00:05:54.605 --> 00:06:00.402
as my wife and my children
were stricken by disease.

40
00:06:00.402 --> 00:06:04.615
I too have cried to the Heavens
for help.

41
00:06:05.908 --> 00:06:11.038
But instead of mercy.
I was met with silence

42
00:06:11.288 --> 00:06:16.502
and the retched sight of my family
suffering like animals...

43
00:06:16.502 --> 00:06:22.174
...until their deaths.
Your gods will no longer mock me!

44
00:06:25.093 --> 00:06:27.137
I will release the Titans.

45
00:06:27.137 --> 00:06:29.723
It's not too late
to end this madness.

46
00:06:29.723 --> 00:06:32.809
Salvation can be yours.
if you wish it.

47
00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:37.397
Let me enlighten you. Priest.

48
00:06:43.862 --> 00:06:47.449
I will end the reign of Gods.

49
00:06:56.375 --> 00:07:00.754
Kolpos Peninsula

50
00:07:02.005 --> 00:07:04.800
You wield that axe well. Theseus.

51
00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:06.426
Maybe some day.

52
00:07:06.426 --> 00:07:10.264
we'll see you use that same
determination to find a wife.

53
00:07:10.472 --> 00:07:14.518
- Are you conspiring with my mother now?
- She worries about you.

54
00:07:14.518 --> 00:07:16.895
There is no need to worry about
me.

55
00:07:17.145 --> 00:07:24.278
You know being a warrior is not just being able
to strike your opponent down with a sword.

56
00:07:24.486 --> 00:07:29.241
It's finding  good reason to draw
your sword in the first place.

57
00:07:29.616 --> 00:07:32.536
I draw my sword
to protect those that I love.

58
00:07:32.786 --> 00:07:36.498
- What about the others?
- They turned their backs on me.

59
00:07:36.498 --> 00:07:41.628
The weak. the defenseless?
Whose going to protect them?

60
00:07:44.715 --> 00:07:49.219
Be careful. too much worry
will make you an old man.
- LOL

61
00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:01.648
Whore!

62
00:08:02.649 --> 00:08:07.696
Last lights for the Holy Labyrinth!

63
00:08:12.242 --> 00:08:16.371
Let the ancestors rest in peace.

64
00:08:36.517 --> 00:08:38.602
Theseus...

65
00:08:45.108 --> 00:08:47.486
Another accident?

66
00:08:48.779 --> 00:08:53.867
Theseus. maybe one day you will
join me in prayer.

67
00:08:53.867 --> 00:08:56.995
Ask the Gods to grant me grandchildren
before I'm too old.

68
00:08:56.995 --> 00:09:01.750
Mother. the gods are children stories.
My spear is not.

69
00:09:02.626 --> 00:09:04.127
You know. mother.

70
00:09:04.127 --> 00:09:07.005
It takes more than lighting candles
to make babies.

71
00:09:07.381 --> 00:09:11.093
Besides the priest wears a ridiculous hat.

72
00:09:45.586 --> 00:09:48.338
- Mother. stay here.
- Theseus...

73
00:10:08.734 --> 00:10:14.364
Fellow Helariks. It is with great
concern that I stand before you.

74
00:10:14.573 --> 00:10:19.203
The Heraklion king. Hyperion.
has seized the Sybelline monastery.

75
00:10:20.204 --> 00:10:22.956
He is only a day's march from here.

76
00:10:22.956 --> 00:10:26.043
We must to evacuate this village immediately!

77
00:10:27.669 --> 00:10:30.005
Quiet. please!

78
00:10:30.255 --> 00:10:32.216
Villagers! We stand no chance!

79
00:10:32.633 --> 00:10:35.302
We stand no chance!

80
00:10:35.594 --> 00:10:37.804
He is delirious from battle.
Please!

81
00:10:38.430 --> 00:10:42.017
We ask every man. woman and child
gather your belongings.

82
00:10:42.017 --> 00:10:44.436
and leave for Mount Tartarus.

83
00:10:44.436 --> 00:10:50.025
Seek refuge behind the safety of the Great Wall.
There. you will be protected.

84
00:10:50.025 --> 00:10:51.193
Anyone that needs more time.

85
00:10:51.193 --> 00:10:55.531
the old. the infirm.
will be escorted in a days' time.

86
00:10:55.489 --> 00:10:58.325
Get ready for departure!

87
00:11:06.416 --> 00:11:09.378
You're with the wrong party.

88
00:11:09.628 --> 00:11:12.339
- Is this not the caravan traveling to Tartarus?
- It is.

89
00:11:12.339 --> 00:11:14.800
But you will not be traveling among us.

90
00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:18.512
- Go in the morning with your own kind.
- My kind?

91
00:11:19.471 --> 00:11:22.808
Peasants & undesirables travel tomorrow.

92
00:11:24.059 --> 00:11:26.895
My kind's blood is the
same color as yours.

93
00:11:26.895 --> 00:11:28.772
Should I spill some to prove it?

94
00:11:28.772 --> 00:11:29.857
Mother!

95
00:11:29.857 --> 00:11:32.609
What happens here?

96
00:11:32.609 --> 00:11:35.737
This bastard
and the whore mother...
FIGHT!!!

97
00:11:43.537 --> 00:11:45.372
Stop!

98
00:11:45.372 --> 00:11:49.126
Fall back!

99
00:11:52.671 --> 00:11:54.715
- Put the sword down!
- I will not!

100
00:11:54.715 --> 00:11:56.925
- Kill him!
- Try and he dies first!

101
00:11:57.801 --> 00:11:59.970
What is it that you want. brother?

102
00:11:59.970 --> 00:12:03.682
It seems as though my kind
travel in the morning.

103
00:12:04.057 --> 00:12:06.518
I want them to have a proper escort.

104
00:12:09.771 --> 00:12:14.193
Move again. and I will bury this
in your skull!

105
00:12:14.193 --> 00:12:16.945
- What's your name?
- Theseus.

106
00:12:16.945 --> 00:12:20.407
Now is not the time for violence Theseus.
Let him go.

107
00:12:20.824 --> 00:12:23.952
Only if I have your word
the rest of the village will be protected.

108
00:12:23.952 --> 00:12:25.913
You have my word.

109
00:12:25.913 --> 00:12:29.124
I will leave capable men for the
caravan tomorrow.

110
00:12:32.002 --> 00:12:34.004
- Kill this traitor!
- I will not have a spectacle!

111
00:12:34.004 --> 00:12:37.883
Restrain him! Get him outta my sight!

112
00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:46.892
Save your blood lust for
Heraklion veins. Theseus.

113
00:12:46.892 --> 00:12:50.729
Join our ranks.
You have been trained well.

114
00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:55.359
I had a good teacher.

115
00:12:55.359 --> 00:12:58.779
I could use a man of your skill at my side
to defeat Hyperion's legions.

116
00:12:58.779 --> 00:13:01.156
Why would I serve you?

117
00:13:01.156 --> 00:13:03.992
You would have so easily abandoned us...

118
00:13:04.201 --> 00:13:06.578
Let's go. Mother.

119
00:13:11.041 --> 00:13:16.296
Lysander. you are no longer part of this army.

120
00:13:17.422 --> 00:13:24.346
Relinquish your shield and your spear and remain here
to travel with the peasants tomorrow.

121
00:13:24.346 --> 00:13:27.057
- But you saw him...
- It is done.

122
00:13:32.896 --> 00:13:34.606
See you later.

123
00:13:37.901 --> 00:13:42.781
Where are your things. old man?
Are you not prepared for the march?

124
00:13:43.365 --> 00:13:50.664
Such odysses were meant for the young people and expectant.
Not for a worn out old goat like me.

125
00:13:50.664 --> 00:13:55.169
Please reconsider.
You know staying here is suicide.

126
00:13:55.419 --> 00:14:00.007
If the Heraklians show up
at least I'll be spared a slow death.

127
00:14:00.007 --> 00:14:05.262
From what I understand. indecision
is not their style.

128
00:14:06.305 --> 00:14:08.599
You are mad.

129
00:14:10.309 --> 00:14:12.519
Just tired...

130
00:14:13.770 --> 00:14:18.901
It's not living as such that's important Theseus.

131
00:14:19.359 --> 00:14:22.946
It's living rightly.

132
00:14:27.826 --> 00:14:31.580
They fight with a ferocity
unlike anything I've seen.

133
00:14:32.372 --> 00:14:35.501
Almost as if they could see in the darkness.

134
00:14:36.543 --> 00:14:39.171
It's always suited them.

135
00:14:39.171 --> 00:14:41.507
You speak as if they are not human.

136
00:14:41.757 --> 00:14:46.470
There are human.
They're Heraklians. they bleed just as we do.

137
00:14:46.470 --> 00:14:53.268
The only difference is they fight for a belief
which allows them to kill without restraint.

138
00:14:53.268 --> 00:14:55.354
That is why they will win.

139
00:14:55.562 --> 00:14:56.855
Lysander...

140
00:14:56.855 --> 00:15:00.692
- I thought Helios ordered you disarmed.
- He did.

141
00:15:38.772 --> 00:15:41.942
Reveal yourself...

142
00:15:54.246 --> 00:15:57.291
Reveal yourself.

143
00:16:00.586 --> 00:16:04.548
- Father...
- Athena...

144
00:16:12.681 --> 00:16:16.226
- Zeus...
- No need for formalities.

145
00:16:16.643 --> 00:16:20.230
None of the other gods are looking?
Are they?

146
00:16:22.441 --> 00:16:24.193
What?

147
00:16:24.193 --> 00:16:28.530
When you walked through here just now.
you actually looked like a father...

148
00:16:28.530 --> 00:16:31.325
...or maybe a grandfather.

149
00:16:32.576 --> 00:16:36.121
We must tread carefully here.
heed the law.

150
00:16:36.121 --> 00:16:39.708
None of the mortals on earth
should witness us in our immortal form.

151
00:16:39.708 --> 00:16:44.963
But father. you've come dangerously close.
You have been influencing the boy Theseus for years.

152
00:16:44.963 --> 00:16:47.049
It is one of them.
never as a god.

153
00:16:47.591 --> 00:16:50.677
Only as his friend.

154
00:16:51.845 --> 00:16:54.097
Why him?

155
00:16:58.435 --> 00:17:01.355
He does not fear danger.

156
00:17:01.813 --> 00:17:06.527
No pain. defeat or ridicule.

157
00:17:06.527 --> 00:17:11.240
He fears only the failure to defend that
which he holds so dear.

158
00:17:13.116 --> 00:17:15.619
His loved ones.

159
00:17:15.869 --> 00:17:19.873
If there is one human who can
lead them against Hyperion.

160
00:17:20.541 --> 00:17:23.335
It would be Theseus.

161
00:17:23.752 --> 00:17:27.047
But it must be his choice.

162
00:17:35.973 --> 00:17:40.978
He defected.
He wants to meet the king.

163
00:18:38.535 --> 00:18:40.204
Up!

164
00:18:53.008 --> 00:18:54.593
Move!

165
00:19:19.785 --> 00:19:22.746
You are a defector from what I understand.

166
00:19:24.289 --> 00:19:27.334
- Yes. my king.
- I am not your king.

167
00:19:28.585 --> 00:19:32.381
But...
I wish you to be.

168
00:19:32.714 --> 00:19:36.426
But you are a traitor by definition.
are you not?

169
00:19:36.885 --> 00:19:39.638
What would I want with a traitor? In my midst.

170
00:19:39.638 --> 00:19:46.353
I can you tell of a village. that lies unprotected.

171
00:19:46.770 --> 00:19:48.981
where you can gather young women...

172
00:19:48.981 --> 00:19:51.108
I have plenty of women.

173
00:19:51.316 --> 00:19:54.945
- Slaves and weaponry...
- I have plenty of weapons.

174
00:19:55.863 --> 00:19:59.658
What I want is the Epirus Bow.

175
00:19:59.658 --> 00:20:06.081
Like this monastery. I have moved every
precious stone you people have worshipped upon...

176
00:20:09.334 --> 00:20:13.172
...and I have yet to find it.

177
00:20:26.977 --> 00:20:30.981
Have you ever met a Sybelline monk. traitor?

178
00:20:30.981 --> 00:20:35.652
The monks of his order are unwavering
in their obedience to the virgin oracle.

179
00:20:35.903 --> 00:20:40.574
With the right prodding. the
Oracle can see where the bow rests.

180
00:20:42.659 --> 00:20:45.370
Couldn't she Monk?

181
00:20:47.289 --> 00:20:50.417
Tell me where she is.

182
00:20:59.343 --> 00:21:02.763
I know your faith. Monk.

183
00:21:03.013 --> 00:21:07.142
Sybellines are forbidden to take a life
under any circumstance.

184
00:21:07.768 --> 00:21:10.145
Even their own.

185
00:21:10.896 --> 00:21:15.234
You have no choice
but to tell me what I want to know.

186
00:21:23.659 --> 00:21:28.372
A monk can be made to talk
with or without his tongue.

187
00:21:28.372 --> 00:21:32.918
Give him to the beast
Make him tell you where the oracle is being kept.

188
00:21:38.173 --> 00:21:43.053
- Do you have any children?
- Not yet.

189
00:21:43.345 --> 00:21:47.349
A man's seed can be his most brutal weapon.

190
00:21:47.349 --> 00:21:52.896
For generations. your people
will stare into the eyes of their sons

191
00:21:52.896 --> 00:21:56.066
and they will see my likeness.

192
00:21:56.441 --> 00:22:00.195
I will be remembered in every glance.

193
00:22:00.195 --> 00:22:03.991
every smile. every tear that is shed for eternity.

194
00:22:03.991 --> 00:22:06.368
But before your baptism.

195
00:22:06.368 --> 00:22:13.584
Understand that you are not drawn here
to my flame... on instinct.

196
00:22:17.421 --> 00:22:22.384
You're here because you are a coward.

197
00:22:23.844 --> 00:22:28.849
and the world does not need anymore cowards.

198
00:22:34.938 --> 00:22:38.108
So I shall do this world a great favor.

199
00:22:38.108 --> 00:22:41.153
And mark you as one of us.

200
00:22:42.029 --> 00:22:46.742
And rid you of the ability to populate the earth.

201
00:22:48.577 --> 00:22:50.787
Traitor!

202
00:22:50.787 --> 00:22:53.665
Although you will not hear them.

203
00:22:55.375 --> 00:22:59.421
Your forefathers weep in their graves.

204
00:22:59.421 --> 00:23:06.929
For the future of their bloodline
ends with you here tonight.

205
00:23:13.810 --> 00:23:16.146
Old man?

206
00:23:17.981 --> 00:23:19.483
Old man!

207
00:23:29.701 --> 00:23:31.703
Hello?

208
00:23:50.389 --> 00:23:52.975
Your anger moves you Theseus.

209
00:23:52.975 --> 00:23:56.478
You must learn to master your emotions.

210
00:23:58.522 --> 00:24:02.276
Rhythm. Theseus. rhythm.

211
00:24:59.875 --> 00:25:01.418
- Noooooooooo!
- Huh?

212
00:25:02.085 --> 00:25:04.004
Theseus!

213
00:25:35.577 --> 00:25:37.579
Wait!

214
00:25:50.676 --> 00:25:53.720
Witness hell!

215
00:26:05.065 --> 00:26:07.317
Not him.

216
00:26:07.943 --> 00:26:12.239
Give him to the jailer.
He can work in the salt mines.

217
00:26:17.494 --> 00:26:20.497
His pain has just begun.

218
00:26:34.469 --> 00:26:38.932
Hyperion's legions show no mercy.

219
00:26:40.976 --> 00:26:46.815
They have destroyed every holy shrine in
their quest for the Epirus Bow.

220
00:26:48.775 --> 00:26:53.238
It is only a matter of time before they find it.

221
00:26:54.281 --> 00:27:00.662
I've noticed their king takes the greatest
care with women that carry a child.

222
00:27:01.788 --> 00:27:05.542
And personally sees to their slaughter.

223
00:27:06.627 --> 00:27:10.672
He ventures to eradicate the Hellenic future.

224
00:27:11.048 --> 00:27:13.425
They honor no rules of engagement.

225
00:27:13.425 --> 00:27:16.303
Effective!
At least. thus far.

226
00:27:16.845 --> 00:27:21.141
Effective? Cowardly.

227
00:27:21.558 --> 00:27:26.271
That may be.
But the Hellenics have yet to adapt.

228
00:27:26.271 --> 00:27:29.233
- And until they do...
- Isn't it time to intervene Zeus?

229
00:27:29.233 --> 00:27:34.738
How can you stomach bearing witness such atrocities
whilst doing nothing?

230
00:27:34.738 --> 00:27:36.240
I obey the law!

231
00:27:36.240 --> 00:27:39.326
No God shall interfere in the affairs of man.

232
00:27:39.326 --> 00:27:42.079
Unless the titans are released.

233
00:27:42.079 --> 00:27:45.457
If we are to expect mankind to have faith in us...

234
00:27:45.457 --> 00:27:48.043
then we must have faith in them.

235
00:27:48.043 --> 00:27:50.921
We must allow them to use their own free-will.

236
00:27:50.921 --> 00:27:53.966
And what if they unearth the Bow?

237
00:27:58.637 --> 00:28:02.432
If any of you come to the aid man

238
00:28:02.724 --> 00:28:07.479
or otherwise influence the
affairs of mankind as a God.

239
00:28:08.313 --> 00:28:11.608
the punishment will be death.

240
00:29:12.461 --> 00:29:17.049
- Who are they?
- The Virgin Oracles!

241
00:29:17.049 --> 00:29:20.344
The Heraklians must have found the temple.

242
00:29:20.385 --> 00:29:23.555
- You don't know of them?
- I don't.

243
00:29:23.555 --> 00:29:26.558
I wouldn't mind knowing them all for a night.

244
00:29:48.580 --> 00:29:53.126
When cloudless skies thunder.
stand fast!

245
00:30:14.731 --> 00:30:19.695
- You are a thief?
- I am a thief my lady.

246
00:30:20.737 --> 00:30:24.366
Were it not for these chains.
I would steal your heart.

247
00:30:24.408 --> 00:30:27.995
Tonight. we must flee this place.

248
00:30:28.579 --> 00:30:31.915
Whichever is strong enough to fight.

249
00:30:33.041 --> 00:30:35.878
- And that man there.
- He didn't even go for the water.

250
00:30:35.919 --> 00:30:38.130
He won't make it to morning.

251
00:30:38.172 --> 00:30:40.841
Just be ready.

252
00:31:06.491 --> 00:31:09.203
Stay apart!

253
00:31:11.121 --> 00:31:13.749
Get inside!

254
00:31:14.166 --> 00:31:16.919
Stay alive...

255
00:31:29.932 --> 00:31:34.895
My Oracle...
You were presented with vision.

256
00:31:34.937 --> 00:31:37.189
What have you seen?

257
00:31:37.940 --> 00:31:40.609
Slave by the water.

258
00:31:42.569 --> 00:31:45.447
He is touched by the Gods.

259
00:31:46.073 --> 00:31:53.080
If he embraces Hyperion.
all of Greece will be destroyed.

260
00:31:55.374 --> 00:31:57.501
Summon the guards.

261
00:32:08.929 --> 00:32:11.515
Only one of them is the true Oracle.

262
00:32:11.557 --> 00:32:15.102
They say that she is pure...

263
00:32:15.394 --> 00:32:18.647
The others are there
to protect her identity.

264
00:32:20.440 --> 00:32:25.571
The virgin Oracle is blessed
with visions of the future.

265
00:32:25.821 --> 00:32:30.534
- If she were to be violated?
- The prophecy would be corrupted.

266
00:32:31.368 --> 00:32:33.912
What a waste...

267
00:33:10.324 --> 00:33:13.911
- Halt!
- Keys!

268
00:33:13.493 --> 00:33:15.287
Run!

269
00:33:15.329 --> 00:33:18.457
We'll take care of guards. Run!

270
00:33:52.658 --> 00:33:55.369
You should get some sleep.

271
00:33:58.997 --> 00:34:02.793
You know I am stronger than I look.

272
00:34:04.795 --> 00:34:07.214
I'll be fine.

273
00:34:13.637 --> 00:34:17.975
Perhaps you have trouble sleeping...

274
00:34:17.975 --> 00:34:22.187
..Because you are haunted
by your visions.

275
00:34:24.147 --> 00:34:27.526
A warrior who reads minds...

276
00:34:33.866 --> 00:34:38.328
Some people do consider my visions
to be a gift.

277
00:34:38.370 --> 00:34:42.124
A gift?
How can they be considered a gift?

278
00:34:42.165 --> 00:34:45.294
You can see the future.
But you do not have the power to change it.

279
00:34:53.677 --> 00:34:56.138
Sorry.

280
00:34:59.683 --> 00:35:02.811
Why would you do such a thing?

281
00:35:03.103 --> 00:35:06.231
You risked your life
to save a complete stranger.

282
00:35:06.273 --> 00:35:09.401
Only faithless man would ask such a question.

283
00:35:09.443 --> 00:35:12.362
My mother was woman of faith.

284
00:35:12.362 --> 00:35:16.450
And her Gods were absent when she needed them the most.

285
00:35:21.747 --> 00:35:23.874
As was I...

286
00:35:26.126 --> 00:35:29.421
So we both mourn?

287
00:35:30.380 --> 00:35:36.553
You. for what has past.
and I. what is to come.

288
00:36:01.537 --> 00:36:04.957
What happened to them?

289
00:36:06.792 --> 00:36:10.212
I gave an order for them not to be touched.

290
00:36:10.254 --> 00:36:12.506
They tried to flee. my king.

291
00:36:12.506 --> 00:36:15.801
Seven of our best men were killed in the struggle.

292
00:36:17.386 --> 00:36:21.849
Seven of your best men.
killed by women?

293
00:36:23.225 --> 00:36:26.979
I wish to know where the Epirus Bow rest.

294
00:36:30.440 --> 00:36:34.069
Which of you can tell me this?

295
00:36:35.445 --> 00:36:39.241
Which of you is the true Oracle?

296
00:36:44.830 --> 00:36:47.666
If I am forced to search you out by other means.

297
00:36:47.666 --> 00:36:50.752
you will experience disomfort.

298
00:36:50.794 --> 00:36:54.965
Discomfort unique to your gender.

299
00:36:55.340 --> 00:37:00.596
So you tell me
which one of you is her.

300
00:37:01.638 --> 00:37:04.141
I am the one you seek.

301
00:37:04.933 --> 00:37:09.563
No. it is I.
I am the one you seek.

302
00:37:11.023 --> 00:37:15.402
The other one said the same thing.
They all claim to be the Oracle.

303
00:37:15.444 --> 00:37:19.531
- The other one?
- Yes. my king.

304
00:37:20.157 --> 00:37:24.077
- The other one? What other one?
- There were four of them.

305
00:37:24.995 --> 00:37:27.206
One of them escaped...

306
00:37:27.915 --> 00:37:31.335
..With a group of slaves
from the watering hole.

307
00:37:44.097 --> 00:37:46.892
- Mondragon?
- Sire.

308
00:37:46.934 --> 00:37:51.522
Find the one that escaped.
Bring her to me alive!

309
00:38:04.409 --> 00:38:07.037
The Dark seas...

310
00:38:08.539 --> 00:38:11.250
These waters are thick with oil.

311
00:38:11.291 --> 00:38:15.546
- and the boat?
- It's a Heraklian merchant ship.

312
00:38:15.754 --> 00:38:18.757
Our best bet is to ambush it
and head south.

313
00:38:18.799 --> 00:38:22.469
- South is not our journey.
- Well it is for me.

314
00:38:25.013 --> 00:38:27.391
From what I hear.

315
00:38:27.432 --> 00:38:33.522
the women down there can get to the meat
of a Malakian chestnut with only their tongues.

316
00:38:35.315 --> 00:38:40.070
Shall you and I test the limits
of that desire. my dear?

317
00:38:40.946 --> 00:38:43.574
The gods have given me vision.

318
00:38:43.615 --> 00:38:46.285
Yet all you do is dream of your appetites

319
00:38:46.326 --> 00:38:48.203
I would rather follow my appetites

320
00:38:48.245 --> 00:38:50.455
than to follow
hallucinations of a harlot.

321
00:38:50.497 --> 00:38:52.916
- She's a high priestess.
- It doesn't matter to me?

322
00:38:52.958 --> 00:38:55.502
A priestess or whore. I'm heading south.

323
00:39:01.049 --> 00:39:04.011
Was it something I said?

324
00:39:05.095 --> 00:39:08.182
Well friend? What will it be?

325
00:39:08.182 --> 00:39:14.813
South with me.
Or will you follow... the lady?

326
00:39:15.981 --> 00:39:17.858
Neither.

327
00:39:20.235 --> 00:39:22.321
I'm taking that ship north

328
00:39:22.321 --> 00:39:25.073
to Hyperion's camp at the monastery.

329
00:39:26.658 --> 00:39:30.871
Your saviour sounds a lot like a mad man to me. Your highness.

330
00:39:32.915 --> 00:39:37.085
Personally. I would rather fight with a madman.
than against him.

331
00:40:08.617 --> 00:40:10.035
Are you minding this?

332
00:40:13.997 --> 00:40:17.459
That is the mortal your father so extolls.
is it not?

333
00:40:23.423 --> 00:40:25.342
And he is with the Oracle.

334
00:40:25.467 --> 00:40:29.805
Poseidon. if Zeus were to suspect you.
we will come to your defense.

335
00:40:47.072 --> 00:40:48.031
Back!

336
00:40:51.326 --> 00:40:53.078
I thought you said this was a merchant ship!

337
00:40:54.788 --> 00:40:56.123
I guess I was wrong!

338
00:40:56.248 --> 00:40:59.334
The sea has forever been an
unpredictable domain...

339
00:41:19.688 --> 00:41:23.901
When the cloudless skies thunders.
stand fast!

340
00:41:25.652 --> 00:41:27.779
- We have to jump now!
- Stand fast!

341
00:42:51.613 --> 00:42:53.615
You knew that wave would save us.

342
00:42:57.452 --> 00:43:02.416
What I see is only a glimmer
of what may come to pass.

343
00:43:03.959 --> 00:43:07.462
Your actions & desires shape what lies ahead.

344
00:43:10.257 --> 00:43:11.842
What else have you seen?

345
00:43:17.222 --> 00:43:20.893
A body wrapped in a shroud. on a rock.

346
00:43:21.435 --> 00:43:25.647
You holding the Epirus Bow and...

347
00:43:30.277 --> 00:43:32.279
embracing Hyperion.

348
00:43:32.446 --> 00:43:36.241
Impossible! I would not embrace
Hyperion!

349
00:43:37.201 --> 00:43:38.619
He killed my mother.

350
00:43:39.953 --> 00:43:44.541
Your mother?
Was she given a proper burial?

351
00:43:47.669 --> 00:43:52.049
No. She still lies where
Hyperion cut her down.

352
00:43:53.258 --> 00:43:57.679
Then you must bury your mother.
Her faith demands it.

353
00:43:58.138 --> 00:44:01.892
- I do not believe in the gods.
- But she believed.

354
00:44:03.477 --> 00:44:06.313
She believed. Theseus.

355
00:44:07.356 --> 00:44:10.067
You must return to your village.

356
00:44:31.338 --> 00:44:34.925
- Have you found the Oracle?
- We did my lord.

357
00:44:35.050 --> 00:44:37.636
But our men were lost before we could recover her.

358
00:44:37.761 --> 00:44:40.055
A storm swept them to sea.

359
00:44:41.098 --> 00:44:45.811
And the Oracle? Did she survive?

360
00:44:46.103 --> 00:44:48.981
She travels towards Kolpos with the slaves.

361
00:44:49.106 --> 00:44:51.316
She could be leading them to the Bow.

362
00:45:00.284 --> 00:45:05.330
Send the beast to Kolpos.
We will go to Tartarus.

363
00:45:05.998 --> 00:45:08.125
- Mondragon!
- Sire...

364
00:45:08.208 --> 00:45:09.668
You stay here.

365
00:45:11.211 --> 00:45:13.422
Set an ambush in the pit.

366
00:46:43.345 --> 00:46:45.848
I'm sorry
I couldn't protect you mother.

367
00:46:50.936 --> 00:46:53.897
But I promise you our family name
will not die with me.

368
00:51:49.943 --> 00:51:52.571
Hyperion's legions are
gathering at Tartarus.

369
00:51:53.280 --> 00:51:55.699
That is where Hellenes will fall.

370
00:51:56.617 --> 00:51:59.244
That future is not set.

371
00:51:59.953 --> 00:52:03.665
But likely.
It will be a slaughter.

372
00:52:04.708 --> 00:52:06.460
You have no faith.

373
00:52:06.752 --> 00:52:08.212
Heathens!

374
00:52:09.338 --> 00:52:13.675
That is true. Darius.
But not always.

375
00:52:14.009 --> 00:52:18.263
When I was just a boy.
I prayed to the gods for a horse

376
00:52:18.722 --> 00:52:23.435
The gods never answered me.
so I stole one instead.

377
00:52:28.315 --> 00:52:31.193
We are surrounded by heathens!

378
00:54:10.834 --> 00:54:14.338
It's alright.
It's alright. Theseus.

379
00:54:16.298 --> 00:54:17.716
What happened to me?

380
00:54:17.966 --> 00:54:21.553
Your arm. You were poisoned.

381
00:54:27.100 --> 00:54:28.644
Where are the others?

382
00:54:29.937 --> 00:54:32.856
They're putting Darius body to rest.

383
00:54:51.416 --> 00:54:53.210
She was right.

384
00:54:56.421 --> 00:54:59.132
For all those years. I doubted it.

385
00:55:01.176 --> 00:55:05.556
I doubted their existence.

386
00:55:06.765 --> 00:55:09.560
Your mother's death
was not in vain. Theseus.

387
00:55:12.062 --> 00:55:16.567
It was fate that brought you back... for the Bow.

388
00:55:20.737 --> 00:55:27.286
With that in your hands Theseus.
it will bring Hellenus victory.

389
00:57:04.716 --> 00:57:09.805
You were right. Theseus.
My visions are a curse.

390
00:57:09.972 --> 00:57:12.975
I want to see the world
through my own eyes.

391
00:57:14.017 --> 00:57:20.023
and feel with my own heart
and to touch with my own flesh.

392
00:57:37.040 --> 00:57:40.043
Hey monk!
I did some "shopping" last night.

393
00:57:40.127 --> 00:57:41.628
Good weapon. huh?

394
00:57:54.975 --> 00:57:57.060
Good to see you're still alive.

395
00:57:57.477 --> 00:58:02.107
- I was worried that cow got the best of you.
- He almost did.

396
00:58:02.566 --> 00:58:04.234
She saved my life.

397
00:58:06.111 --> 00:58:08.363
Looks like she did more than that.

398
00:58:12.451 --> 00:58:14.119
Careful...

399
00:58:14.328 --> 00:58:17.915
Just because you have that bow.
doesn't mean I'm gonna treat you any differently.

400
00:58:18.373 --> 00:58:21.710
Good. We march to the monastery.

401
00:58:23.378 --> 00:58:25.214
We have a war to fight.

402
00:58:25.839 --> 00:58:29.092
Mount Tartarus

403
00:58:29.218 --> 00:58:34.306
The faithful believe the Titans are
still buried deep within the mountains.

404
00:58:39.561 --> 00:58:45.025
The Great Wall is the Hellenecs only hope
against your army.

405
00:58:51.198 --> 00:58:52.533
Defences?

406
00:58:52.658 --> 00:58:57.788
Originally. there was a dam.
but the Hellenecs have since adapted it.

407
00:58:58.914 --> 00:59:03.335
No one could have anticipated
the enemy you have become.

408
00:59:04.002 --> 00:59:05.504
How many are there?

409
00:59:05.963 --> 00:59:08.882
How many have made it here. Your Majesty.
I'm not sure.

410
00:59:09.174 --> 00:59:13.345
- How many?
- I'm not sure. Your Majesty.

411
00:59:15.097 --> 00:59:17.766
- 800.
- And the gate?

412
00:59:17.891 --> 00:59:22.896
20 feet of marble stone.
weighing over 12 tons.

413
00:59:23.021 --> 00:59:26.108
It was designed to be
impenetrable. your majesty.

414
00:59:27.025 --> 00:59:33.699
Have you known of a gate
designed to be anything but?

415
00:59:44.001 --> 00:59:46.295
Go be of service somewhere else.

416
01:00:03.687 --> 01:00:05.314
Where is he?!

417
01:00:05.564 --> 01:00:07.858
I thought Hyperion was suppose to be camped here.

418
01:00:07.983 --> 01:00:09.526
We should continue.

419
01:00:09.651 --> 01:00:12.654
Tartarus is another two days
along this ridge.

420
01:00:13.697 --> 01:00:15.449
What is that sound?

421
01:00:45.729 --> 01:00:49.149
Stay down! Stavros. help me!

422
01:00:49.650 --> 01:00:51.443
Stay down!

423
01:00:54.404 --> 01:00:56.865
No!

424
01:00:58.367 --> 01:01:02.621
My sisters!
My sisters!

425
01:01:02.788 --> 01:01:04.331
They're in the bull!

426
01:01:10.671 --> 01:01:14.633
No! My sisters!

427
01:01:16.593 --> 01:01:19.805
I am the Oracle!

428
01:01:25.060 --> 01:01:28.605
- I am the Oracle.
- I'm also looking for.

429
01:01:28.730 --> 01:01:31.441
I am Oracle...

430
01:01:33.318 --> 01:01:36.738
Theseus! They are still here.

431
01:01:43.453 --> 01:01:45.163
Wait! Monk!

432
01:01:46.707 --> 01:01:48.041
It's a trap!

433
01:02:03.098 --> 01:02:04.474
Monk!

434
01:02:22.826 --> 01:02:24.453
Theseus!

435
01:03:08.163 --> 01:03:10.207
Do not stop until you reach Tartarus.

436
01:03:10.290 --> 01:03:12.543
The horses will run
until their hearts give out.

437
01:03:12.668 --> 01:03:16.380
Hyperion will soon have the Bow.
Leave!

438
01:03:42.072 --> 01:03:45.158
Forgive me. Father!

439
01:03:46.785 --> 01:03:50.038
I only broke the law
to protect the mortal.

440
01:04:30.454 --> 01:04:34.166
No God will ever again come to your aid!

441
01:04:34.833 --> 01:04:37.336
You are on your own!

442
01:04:39.171 --> 01:04:42.216
Do you understand. mortal?

443
01:04:43.342 --> 01:04:45.719
I have faith in you. Theseus.

444
01:04:46.053 --> 01:04:52.643
Prove me right!
Lead your people!

445
01:05:34.309 --> 01:05:35.519
Halt!

446
01:05:52.411 --> 01:05:54.997
The horse I prayed for when I was a boy.

447
01:05:55.163 --> 01:05:56.790
What is wrong with them?

448
01:05:59.126 --> 01:06:00.711
They're dying.

449
01:06:22.149 --> 01:06:26.862
- Where are the men?
- They have yet to return. sire.

450
01:06:27.279 --> 01:06:30.324
What does the sign on the bird tell you?

451
01:06:33.994 --> 01:06:35.579
Speak.

452
01:06:37.539 --> 01:06:39.208
The Gods...

453
01:06:40.918 --> 01:06:45.672
- They came from above.
- The Gods?

454
01:06:45.756 --> 01:06:48.634
They appeared
and laid waste to the men. my king.

455
01:06:50.677 --> 01:06:53.430
The Gods...

456
01:06:57.267 --> 01:07:00.771
They protected the slave who
travels with the Oracle.

457
01:07:03.815 --> 01:07:06.860
The Gods fight on their behalf. sire.

458
01:07:11.865 --> 01:07:14.868
If the men hear of this.
there will be panic.

459
01:07:15.327 --> 01:07:18.956
I know...

460
01:08:06.378 --> 01:08:10.174
In peace.
sons bury their fathers.

461
01:08:10.966 --> 01:08:15.012
In war.
fathers bury their sons.

462
01:08:22.811 --> 01:08:24.605
Are we at war. father?

463
01:09:05.270 --> 01:09:07.189
I have important information
for the Council.

464
01:09:07.314 --> 01:09:11.235
Theseus! I know this man.
Let him through.

465
01:09:17.241 --> 01:09:19.368
I hope you've come to join the fight.

466
01:09:31.880 --> 01:09:33.924
Where's the army?

467
01:09:43.642 --> 01:09:45.435
Tell me about the slave.

468
01:09:48.146 --> 01:09:50.941
He's from your village. is he not?

469
01:09:52.484 --> 01:09:54.820
- Answer me!
- Yes.

470
01:09:55.904 --> 01:09:58.156
He was a peasant.

471
01:10:01.535 --> 01:10:03.412
As was I.

472
01:10:04.580 --> 01:10:08.417
- Forgive me. Your Majesty. I meant no...
- Quiet.

473
01:10:08.876 --> 01:10:11.086
And his family?

474
01:10:11.795 --> 01:10:14.756
His mother was raped
by some villagers.

475
01:10:14.840 --> 01:10:16.925
Nobody would marry her.

476
01:10:18.260 --> 01:10:20.762
He was a bastard.

477
01:10:24.141 --> 01:10:26.018
And his name?

478
01:10:26.602 --> 01:10:31.440
- Theseus.
- Very well. I'll meet him.

479
01:10:41.200 --> 01:10:44.286
Helios tells me
that you have information useful to us.

480
01:10:44.369 --> 01:10:46.705
Hyperion is in possession
of the Epirus Bow.

481
01:10:48.332 --> 01:10:51.084
- The Epirus Bow?
- Yes. the weapon forged by Hercules.

482
01:10:51.168 --> 01:10:53.795
I heard the same stories you did as a child.

483
01:10:53.921 --> 01:10:58.217
Gods in living in the clouds
and Titans buried in rocks...

484
01:10:58.300 --> 01:11:01.637
Listen! I was a disbeliever
just like you are.

485
01:11:01.803 --> 01:11:03.472
But the Epirus Bow exists.

486
01:11:03.597 --> 01:11:08.268
I understand that there are many Hellenecs
who put great faith in the myths and the gods.

487
01:11:08.393 --> 01:11:11.104
but we in the Hellenac Council do not.

488
01:11:11.271 --> 01:11:14.316
They are metaphors son.
nothing more.

489
01:11:14.399 --> 01:11:18.570
We are a society of  laws
based on negotiation and reason.

490
01:11:18.695 --> 01:11:22.115
If you try to negotiate with Hyperion.
you will be the death of us all.

491
01:11:22.241 --> 01:11:27.955
If I were to accept your council.
Theseus from Kolpos. what would it be?

492
01:11:28.038 --> 01:11:30.707
Seal the gates
and prepare for war!

493
01:11:30.832 --> 01:11:32.501
We have Happolyt battalions returning.

494
01:11:32.584 --> 01:11:33.377
We can't seal the gates.

495
01:11:33.460 --> 01:11:36.296
No one will return!
We are the last!

496
01:11:36.630 --> 01:11:39.258
I'm sure you'll understand
if I do not accept the advice

497
01:11:39.341 --> 01:11:43.178
of an alluring palm reader
and her peasant lover.

498
01:11:44.137 --> 01:11:47.015
Sir. a Heraklian envoy approaches.

499
01:11:50.143 --> 01:11:54.273
There. you see? No ruler
wishes for war.

500
01:11:54.398 --> 01:11:58.861
They only wish to be taken seriously
at the bargaining table.

501
01:11:59.111 --> 01:12:02.072
Alert the Council
and prepare a delegation.

502
01:12:06.368 --> 01:12:07.703
Bows!

503
01:12:11.331 --> 01:12:12.666
Stop!

504
01:12:15.377 --> 01:12:16.920
Stop!

505
01:12:17.296 --> 01:12:20.048
Remain still.
or we will be forced to fire upon you!

506
01:12:23.844 --> 01:12:26.346
extend your arms outward!

507
01:12:29.349 --> 01:12:31.977
He bears the olive branch
of peace.

508
01:12:32.853 --> 01:12:37.608
My king wishes to speak
with the one called Theseus from Kolpos.

509
01:12:41.653 --> 01:12:43.280
Theseus!

510
01:12:45.365 --> 01:12:48.452
Hyperion's envoy desires a word with you.

511
01:12:49.870 --> 01:12:53.957
Like the vision.
He sends for you with arms open.

512
01:12:54.917 --> 01:12:58.921
- Seeking an embrace of loyalty.
- Phaedra...

513
01:13:00.422 --> 01:13:02.090
Have you never been wrong?

514
01:13:15.270 --> 01:13:17.731
We can't protect you beyond this gate.

515
01:13:23.695 --> 01:13:25.864
I am Theseus!

516
01:13:26.031 --> 01:13:29.743
Come closer.
I have a message for you.

517
01:13:29.952 --> 01:13:31.745
Don't risk it.

518
01:13:36.124 --> 01:13:38.418
At worst. you lose a peasant.

519
01:13:47.636 --> 01:13:51.056
- Better?
- Yes.

520
01:13:52.015 --> 01:13:53.809
Why do you cover your face?

521
01:13:53.892 --> 01:13:56.770
All are equal in
Hyperion's midst.

522
01:13:56.895 --> 01:14:01.108
I myself am only a vessel for
of his demands. nothing more.

523
01:14:01.233 --> 01:14:05.195
- And he ask me by name?
- Indeed he does.

524
01:14:05.279 --> 01:14:06.363
And how does he know it?

525
01:14:06.446 --> 01:14:09.449
Theseus. there is little the king
does not know.

526
01:14:09.533 --> 01:14:15.205
He knows that you have no father. and like him.
you were cast aside by your very own people.

527
01:14:15.497 --> 01:14:17.541
Does he know of my rage?

528
01:14:18.292 --> 01:14:21.587
Does he know that I live only to see
his blood on the end of my sword?

529
01:14:21.670 --> 01:14:24.631
Does he know that he butchered my mother?

530
01:14:32.139 --> 01:14:36.643
Now that. he's seen your face. he knows.

531
01:14:45.194 --> 01:14:47.321
You wouldn't make it.

532
01:14:47.988 --> 01:14:49.615
Coward!

533
01:14:49.740 --> 01:14:55.245
Embrace me. Theseus.
They will never give you a say at their table.

534
01:14:55.537 --> 01:14:58.540
But you could sit at the head of mine.

535
01:14:58.916 --> 01:15:00.584
Long after this war is over.

536
01:15:00.667 --> 01:15:04.880
My mark will be left on
this world forever.

537
01:15:06.840 --> 01:15:10.636
The sun will never set
on my blood. Theseus.

538
01:15:10.719 --> 01:15:14.765
This is what I offer you. immortality.

539
01:15:15.098 --> 01:15:19.186
Deeds are eternal. not the flesh.

540
01:15:23.190 --> 01:15:27.361
The Gods may be on your side. but tomorrow...

541
01:15:28.070 --> 01:15:30.280
..I unleash the Titans.

542
01:15:34.201 --> 01:15:38.413
- What was discussed?
- Seal the gate.

543
01:15:38.539 --> 01:15:42.417
- What were his demands?
- Seal the gate.

544
01:15:43.210 --> 01:15:45.003
Theseus!

545
01:16:01.270 --> 01:16:04.064
He is Theseus?

546
01:16:11.154 --> 01:16:14.700
- That was him. wasn't it?
- I was that close!

547
01:16:46.148 --> 01:16:49.234
I don't know if I can do
what Zeus asks me.

548
01:16:52.446 --> 01:16:55.866
By doubting. one comes to truth. Theseus.

549
01:16:59.411 --> 01:17:02.164
The gods chose well.

550
01:18:49.897 --> 01:18:53.400
Sir! There is movement on the front.

551
01:19:16.548 --> 01:19:18.342
What is he holding?

552
01:19:21.720 --> 01:19:22.930
A Bow!

553
01:19:39.863 --> 01:19:41.740
Fall back!

554
01:19:42.533 --> 01:19:46.411
Run!

555
01:19:49.456 --> 01:19:54.628
Do not go back! Hold!

556
01:20:07.391 --> 01:20:08.809
Listen to me!

557
01:20:12.187 --> 01:20:13.814
Listen!

558
01:20:16.817 --> 01:20:19.319
Who are you to tell us what to do?

559
01:20:19.444 --> 01:20:23.615
I am nobody to tell you what to do!
I am Theseus. a good man.

560
01:20:23.740 --> 01:20:25.909
One of you.
I share your blood

561
01:20:25.993 --> 01:20:28.537
and I share your fear!

562
01:20:28.704 --> 01:20:32.207
But to run now.
we offer our souls

563
01:20:32.332 --> 01:20:36.044
and the souls of our children
to a terrible darkness.

564
01:20:45.888 --> 01:20:49.141
Hold! We must stand and fight!

565
01:20:49.224 --> 01:20:51.518
Their numbers count for nothing in the tunnel!

566
01:20:51.643 --> 01:20:53.187
Stand your ground!

567
01:20:55.022 --> 01:20:56.940
Stand your ground!

568
01:21:01.069 --> 01:21:04.698
Just because they have scold
their faces and scarred their bodies.

569
01:21:04.823 --> 01:21:08.952
does not mean they are braver
or stronger than we are.

570
01:21:09.620 --> 01:21:13.665
They are cowards!
They hide behind their masks!

571
01:21:13.832 --> 01:21:18.003
There are human and they bleed
like you and I.

572
01:21:24.176 --> 01:21:25.427
Listen to me!

573
01:21:26.595 --> 01:21:28.222
Stand your ground!

574
01:21:28.597 --> 01:21:30.098
Fight for honor!

575
01:21:30.599 --> 01:21:34.561
Fight for the man beside you.
fight for those who bore you!

576
01:21:34.770 --> 01:21:36.563
Fight for your children!

577
01:21:36.730 --> 01:21:38.607
Fight for your future!

578
01:21:38.774 --> 01:21:41.068
Fight for your name! Survive!

579
01:21:41.193 --> 01:21:42.778
Fight...

580
01:21:43.612 --> 01:21:45.948
..For immortality!

581
01:21:52.871 --> 01:21:56.166
Let us write history with Heraklian blood!

582
01:22:03.924 --> 01:22:07.010
Company!

583
01:23:30.886 --> 01:23:32.221
King Hyperion...

584
01:23:33.972 --> 01:23:35.766
We can negotiate.

585
01:23:36.642 --> 01:23:38.018
I see no reason to...

586
01:23:46.068 --> 01:23:48.362
Theseus!

587
01:23:49.530 --> 01:23:50.989
Where are you?

588
01:23:51.114 --> 01:23:53.033
Theseus of Kolpos!

589
01:23:56.286 --> 01:23:59.122
- Where is your king?
- He is not king!

590
01:24:20.394 --> 01:24:22.145
Stavros. the shrine!

591
01:24:45.544 --> 01:24:48.297
Theseus. I'm right behind you!

592
01:25:05.397 --> 01:25:06.523
Phaedra!

593
01:25:09.318 --> 01:25:12.738
Phaedra! Stay in the shrine!

594
01:25:44.686 --> 01:25:46.104
Hyperion!

595
01:25:58.075 --> 01:25:59.326
No!

596
01:26:29.815 --> 01:26:31.233
Theseus!

597
01:26:34.695 --> 01:26:36.154
Theseus!

598
01:26:56.925 --> 01:26:58.427
Theseus!

599
01:27:01.555 --> 01:27:03.182
I got the Bow!

600
01:27:03.807 --> 01:27:05.309
Stavros...

601
01:27:07.269 --> 01:27:08.645
I got the Bow!

602
01:27:12.482 --> 01:27:13.525
I'll hold them back!

603
01:27:13.609 --> 01:27:16.403
- Stavros...
- Get out!

604
01:27:16.486 --> 01:27:19.406
I got the bow!
I'll hold them while I can!

605
01:27:19.573 --> 01:27:21.241
Get out of here. now!

606
01:27:27.372 --> 01:27:29.875
Which one of you comes for me huh?

607
01:27:59.571 --> 01:28:02.282
None of you
will leave this place.

608
01:28:17.089 --> 01:28:18.590
Leave here!

609
01:28:19.424 --> 01:28:21.635
This is no longer your fight!

610
01:28:23.595 --> 01:28:25.264
Find Hyperion!

611
01:30:00.984 --> 01:30:03.278
Die with your gods.

612
01:32:21.542 --> 01:32:23.126
Athena!

613
01:32:50.445 --> 01:32:51.613
Father!

614
01:32:54.700 --> 01:32:57.202
Do not forsake my kind.

615
01:34:19.576 --> 01:34:21.912
What does it feel like knowing...

616
01:34:23.497 --> 01:34:26.583
..knowing that there will be no memory of you?

617
01:34:27.876 --> 01:34:29.545
I've won.

618
01:34:31.630 --> 01:34:35.092
My death. will make me
a legend.

619
01:34:44.184 --> 01:34:45.769
And my deeds...

620
01:34:47.688 --> 01:34:49.857
..Will go down in history!

621
01:34:56.613 --> 01:34:58.824
I'm writing your history.

622
01:35:24.808 --> 01:35:26.977
Do it!

623
01:35:43.744 --> 01:35:49.416
This is your last embrace. Hyperion.

624
01:35:53.879 --> 01:35:55.130
Look at me!

625
01:35:57.257 --> 01:35:59.301
Look at me!

626
01:36:00.844 --> 01:36:02.513
I am the last thing...

627
01:36:03.722 --> 01:36:05.557
..You will ever see.

628
01:36:09.311 --> 01:36:13.023
Witness hell!

629
01:38:34.957 --> 01:38:39.169
All men's souls are immortal.

630
01:38:41.547 --> 01:38:47.761
But the souls of the righteous
are immortal and divine.

631
01:38:52.099 --> 01:38:54.643
Once an faithless man.

632
01:38:54.852 --> 01:38:59.147
Theseus gave his life
to save mankind.

633
01:38:59.314 --> 01:39:02.901
and earned a place
amongst the gods.

634
01:39:04.987 --> 01:39:08.240
They rewarded his bravery
with a gift:

635
01:39:08.824 --> 01:39:12.077
a son. Acamas.

636
01:39:43.609 --> 01:39:46.862
Don't be afraid of your visions. little one.

637
01:39:48.197 --> 01:39:50.991
- What's your name?
- Acamas.

638
01:39:51.617 --> 01:39:53.327
Acamas?

639
01:39:54.578 --> 01:39:56.496
A strong name...

640
01:39:58.999 --> 01:40:04.171
I knew your father.
He was a very brave man.

641
01:40:07.341 --> 01:40:09.218
Soon...

642
01:40:09.760 --> 01:40:12.095
..It will be your time.

643
01:40:13.305 --> 01:40:14.932
My time for what?

644
01:40:15.015 --> 01:40:17.851
The fight against evil
never ends. Acamas.

645
01:40:17.935 --> 01:40:20.687
War is coming to the Heavens.

646
01:40:22.231 --> 01:40:27.611
And your father will be there.
Fighting for your future.

647
01:40:30.405 --> 01:40:33.450
Acamas!

648
01:40:38.497 --> 01:40:40.582
- How quickly he's grown!
- I know.

649
01:40:41.625 --> 01:40:43.168
Who was that son?

650
01:40:47.422 --> 01:40:49.216
Just an old man...

651
01:40:50.305 --> 01:41:50.942
